# Managed by Ansible - do not edit manually
# Local-IPC AF_UNIX socket grant - /etc/apparmor.d/abstractions/local_mixin_network_local_ipc
#
# Include in EVERY confined GUI app. At abi/4.0+ AppArmor mediates AF_UNIX (local
# inter-process sockets) SEPARATELY from the coarse `network` rule, and a bare `network,`
# (or abstractions/base / abstractions/nameservice) no longer implies it. Wayland (display),
# D-Bus (IPC / notifications), PipeWire / Pulse (audio) and journald (logging) all run over
# AF_UNIX, so the moment a profile pins `abi <abi/5.0>` these are default-denied unless granted
# here - the app loses display, IPC, audio and logging.
#
# AF_UNIX is local-by-definition and carries NO network egress, so granting it does not widen
# the egress surface that local_mixin_network_app (whitelist) / local_mixin_network_deny (block)
# control - both of those include this mixin; a no-egress viewer still needs local IPC.
#
# stream = Wayland / D-Bus / X11 / audio control sockets. dgram = journald log socket.
# Only effective at an abi that mediates AF_UNIX (abi/4.0+); managed profiles pin `abi <abi/5.0>`.

network unix stream,
network unix dgram,
